  "id": "COMPOUND:28245 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a consistent relationship between 7-Hydroxy-2-(4-Hydroxyphenyl)Chromen-4-One and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as all three entities are linked through a series of targets. The drug appears to interact with DMS-79, which in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, indicating a potential mechanism of action involving DMS-79 as a mediator. The evidence is supported by multiple pathways, each linking the compound to the complex through different intermediates, suggesting a broader biological context where the compound may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex via DMS-79. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in modulating the activity of the polycomb group (PcG) proteins, which are involved in epigenetic regulation. The mechanism is further supported by the presence of multiple targets, indicating a possible role in the regulation of gene expression through the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex.",
